#%PAM-1.0
# shani-shell lock screen, the second conversation: face (linux-hello, an IR
# camera), then fingerprint (fprintd), then a security key (pam-u2f), beside the
# password one - a look or a touch unlocks while the password field still works.
# A module that is not installed is skipped; with none, this always fails and the
# password stays. pam_u2f with nouserok and no registered key, or no key plugged
# in, falls through (measured with pam-u2f 1.4.0) - never a way in on its own.
-auth      sufficient   pam_linux_hello.so timeout=4000 quiet
-auth      sufficient   pam_fprintd.so max-tries=3 timeout=30
-auth      sufficient   pam_u2f.so cue [cue_prompt=Touch your security key] nouserok
auth       requisite    pam_deny.so
